details:
(a) the details of measures taken by Government to provide social security and health insurance coverage to unorganised sector workers registered on e-Shram Portal during the last three years;
(b) the status of implementation of Central schemes for generating new employment opportunities and promoting skill development among youth in the country, State-wise; and
(c) whether Government proposes to revise the national minimum wage rates for unorganised workers and if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether National Commission for Women (NCW) has taken suo motu cognizance of indecent and gender-insensitive remarks made against women in stand-up comedy and on digital platforms;
(b) the current status of the proposed amendment bill to include digital and online content within the ambit of the 'Indecent Representation of Women (Prohibition) Act, 1986';
(c) the details of the awareness campaigns being run to ensure the dignity, consent and safety of women in entertainment media; and
(d) whether an inter-ministerial task force has been constituted in collaboration with the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Ministry of Information and Broadcasting to curb the objectification of women in cyberspace?

(a) the number of Anganwadi Centres upgraded under the Saksham Anganwadi scheme in Maharashtra and the status of drinking water and toilet facilities therein;
(b) the official figures indicating the reduction in the number of children suffering from malnutrition and Severe Acute Malnutrition (SAM) in the State under POSHAN 2.0; and
(c) the number of women in the State who have received Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) under the Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana (PMMVY) under Mission Shakti (Sambal and Samarth)?

(a) whether Government has conducted any study on the impact of port-led industrialization and connectivity projects under the 'Sagarmala Programme';
(b) the present status of cargo traffic on major National Waterways across the country and the incentives being provided to promote the same;
(c) the progress made under 'Maritime India Vision 2030' towards bringing the turnaround time of Indian ports at par with global benchmarks; and
(d) the policies being adopted to attract private investment in coastal shipping and inland water transport?

(a) whether Government has formulated any concrete policy to provide relief to common citizens from inflation in the country and to control the prices of essential commodities;
(b) the mechanism in place to ensure the quality and transparency of foodgrains being distributed through Public Distribution System (PDS);
(c) the extent of benefits accrued to migrant workers in the country so far under the 'One Nation One Ration Card' (ONORC) scheme; and
(d) the details of steps taken by Government to ensure the timely delivery of free foodgrains to the last mile beneficiary in rural areas?

(a) the percentage of rural households in the country that have been provided with safe drinking water through tap connections under the Jal Jeevan Mission so far;
(b) the special budget allocated to improve ground water levels in water-stressed districts;
(c) the mechanism put in place for quality testing of water supplied through taps; and
(d) the new projects approved to enhance irrigation facilities for farmers in drought affected areas?

(a) whether Government has evaluated the socio-economic impact of regional air connectivity in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities under the UDAN scheme;
(b) the total number of air routes currently operational under the scheme and the details of routes that have proven to be financially unviable (non-operational);
(c) the incentives being offered to ensure the financial stability of regional airlines and to attract private investment; and
(d) the current status of green airport initiatives aimed at reducing carbon emissions?

(a) the present physical status of the development of the Delhi–Mumbai Industrial Corridor (DMIC) and the Shendra–Bidkin Industrial Area in Maharashtra;
(b) the budgetary provisions made for the development of cold chain infrastructure and cargo hubs for the export of fruits from Nashik, Jalgaon and Nagpur;
(c) the details of the Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) received by Maharashtra during the last three years, sector-wise; and
(d) the policy initiatives taken to integrate the Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) of the State with the global supply chain?
GK

(a) the action plan prepared by the Ministry for archaeological conservation and international promotion of 12 historical forts in Maharashtra and Tamil Nadu that have been included in the UNESCO World Heritage List under the 'Maratha Military Landscapes';
(b) whether Government proposes to develop modern infrastructure, accessible approach roads and world-class civic amenities for tourists visiting these global heritage sites; and
(c) the details of the special budgetary provisions made in the current financial year for restoration and security of these forts under the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI)?

(a) the progress made so far in providing cashless health cover of up to 5 lakh rupees to the underprivileged families of the country under Ayushman Bharat-Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY), the details thereof, State-wise;
(b) the positive socio-economic benefits derived from this scheme in saving poor families from the burden of heavy medical expenses and debt; and
(c) the role this scheme played in strengthening medical infrastructure and tertiary health services in Tier-2 and Tier-3 cities?

(a) the current status of anemia control among pregnant and reproductive-age women in Maharashtra and the manner in which it is encouraging as compared to the national average;
(b) the detail of the innovative 'TRACK' component under the 'Anemia Mukt Bharat' guidelines and the status of its implementation in Maharashtra, district-wise;
(c) the details of the availability and usage of life-saving intravenous iron therapy for managing severe anemia cases in community health centers and district hospitals in Maharashtra; and
(d) the effective measures being taken by Government to ensure 100 per cent compliance with the 180-day Iron-Folic Acid supplementation and to increase awareness?

(a) the State-wise details of houses sanctioned and completed so far across the country, including the State of Maharashtra, under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban 2.0 and the proportion of sole or co-ownership by women under the scheme;
(b)the details of the progress of budget utilization for the Financial Year 2025-26 and the factors contributing to positive outcomes;
(c) Maharashtra's allocated share out of the ?3,000 crore earmarked in the Union Budget 2026-27; and
(d) the steps taken by Government to expedite administrative processes in order to ensure prompt financial benefits and ownership rights for women beneficiaries?

(a) the special measures being taken to facilitate loan sanction for artisans trained under the PM Vishwakarma Scheme;
(b) whether any bank-wise coordination mechanism is put in place to meet the credit requirements of Paithani weavers and Kolhapuri chappal artisans of the State of Maharashtra;
(c) the district-wise details of the artisans benefited so far in Kolhapur, Nashik and Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar; and
(d) the future plans for protecting GI-tagged products from counterfeit goods and for Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) for raw materials?

(a) whether the attention of Government has been drawn towards the inordinate delay in expansion of new railway lines and execution of pending railway projects in the Nagpur, Solapur and Marathwada divisions of Maharashtra;
(b) whether there is any proposal to introduce additional air-conditioned (AC) suburban train services and to upgrade the infrastructure in view of the increasing passenger congestion and safety concerns in the Mumbai Suburban Railway and the Central Railway; and
(c) whether any proposal is under consideration for the modernisation of major railway stations under the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme and introduce new Vande Bharat Express train services connecting major economic centres of Maharashtra?

(a) the plan to provide targeted social security through a 'one-stop solution' after the number of women among the more than 31.5 crore unorganized workers registered on the e-Shram portal crossed a record 54 percent;
(b) whether Government is ensuring direct benefit transfer to unorganized women workers across the country, including Maharashtra in agriculture, domestic work and construction sectors by linking them with the 'Palna' Scheme and 'Pradhan Mantri Shram Yogi Maandhan Yojana' pension scheme; and
(c) the special budgetary provisions made by the Ministry for skill development, maternity benefits and safe working environment (WASH infrastructure) for such women workers?

(a) the success achieved under the Khelo India Scheme in providing state-of-the-art sports facilities to the rural and tribal youth of Maharashtra;
(b) the current status of registration of youth from the State on MY Bharat Portal and their leadership development; and
(c) the policy for preparing sportspersons from the State for global competitions through the Target Olympic Podium Scheme (TOPS)?

(a) the progress made under the Pradhan Mantri Viksit Bharat Rozgar Yojana (PMVBRY) regarding the financial incentives being provided to first-time formal workers registered with the EPFO ??across the country, including Maharashtra;
(b) the success achieved in connecting unorganized and construction workers with the social security benefits in lumpsum through the e-Shram portal and its new mobile app in Maharashtra; and
(c) the steps taken to provide employment opportunities to the youth in aspirational districts in Maharashtra through coordination between the NCS portal and the Digital Skill India Hub?

(a) the details of the uninterrupted actual supply of Urea and DAP ensured by Government during the Kharif and Rabi seasons in Maharashtra against the record demand, district-wise;
(b) the manner in which Government, while taking prompt action on complaints regarding the forced bundling (linking) of other products with fertilizers and black marketing by local dealers, has eliminated this malpractice through the transparent Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) system; and
(c) the policy being adopted under the 'One Nation One Fertilizer' scheme to enhance the availability of affordable Nano Urea and create public awareness thereof in remote rural areas?

(a) percentage of rural households in the country, particularly in Maharashtra, currently receiving the actual benefit of 'Har Ghar Jal' under the 'Jal Jeevan Mission' and the new timeline for covering the remaining households;
(b) whether Government is bridging the gap between infrastructure (tap connections) and actual water supply and taking steps to address technical shortcomings responsible for irregular supply of water through taps due to shortage of water sources; and
(c) details of the action plan of Government to address challenges/bottlenecks such as declining groundwater levels, lack of operation and maintenance (O&M) and negligence on the part of contractors?

(a) the details of the record 95 airports and heliports operationalized so far across the country under the historic success of the UDAN scheme, State-wise;
(b) whether Government has any plan to further strengthen connectivity by developing night landing and other modern facilities at strategic hubs such as Solapur airport; and
(c) the upcoming roadmap to connect 120 new regional airports over the coming decade?

(a) the special steps being taken under the 'Pradhan Mantri Mega Integrated Textile Region and Apparel' (PM MITRA) scheme to make the Solapur textile cluster in Maharashtra globally competitive;
(b) the number of local weavers and women artisans in Solapur provided with modern technical training and employment under the Samarth Scheme during the last three years; and
(c) whether Government is providing international marketing assistance under the 'One District One Product' (ODOP) initiative to promote the export of the famous 'GI Tagged' bedsheets and towels of Solapur?

(a) whether Government has formulated any special incentive schemes to make onion farmers in major districts like Nashik and Ahmednagar of Maharashtra globally competitive and to bring about their economic empowerment; 
(b) the outcomes in terms of strengthening the reputation and share of Indian onion in traditional international markets following the historic decision to remove export duty on onion in April, 2025; and 
(c) whether Government is considering formulating a permanent, sustainable and transparent export policy to safeguard farmers' income and maintain a balance in the interests of consumers, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government intends to widen the smart classroom coverage in Kendriya Vidyalayas of other States including Maharashtra under the PM e-Vidya or Digital India initiatives; 
(b) if so, the timeline for such expansion and the amount of funds to be allocated therefor, the details thereof; 
(c) likely number of additional classes or schools to be included under this program; and 
(d) if so, the details thereof in respect of the State of Maharashtra?
J

(a) the number of functional primary, district and apex cooperative societies in the State of Maharashtra as on date, category-wise;
(b) the quantum of Central assistance released to the State of Maharashtra under cooperative sector reform and digitalisation schemes during the last three years;
(c) the measures taken by the Central Government to strengthen dairy, sugar and agricultural cooperative societies in Maharashtra, particularly in drought-affected districts; and
(d) the details thereof in respect of the State of Maharashtra?
J

(a) the total installed renewable energy capacity in the State of Maharashtra;
(b) the steps taken by Government to promote solar energy in the tribal areas of the State;
(c) the details thereof and the incentives provided for the installation of rooftop solar panels;
(d) the progress of wind and hybrid energy projects; and
(e) the future targets for green energy generation in the State and the details thereof?

(a) the recent steps taken by Government to strengthen primary healthcare services and promote disease prevention in the country and the details thereof;
(b) the details of recent policies/programmes relating to Ayushman Bharat, digital health and maternal and child health in the State of Maharashtra; and
(c) the improvements made so far in accessing healthcare services, their quality and public health indicators as a result of these initiatives and the State-wise details thereof, particularly in respect of the State of Maharashtra?

(a) whether Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Urban (PMAY-U) 2.0 and other urban housing schemes have been implemented to ensure "Housing for All" across various States of the country;
(b) if so, the State-wise/year-wise number of houses sanctioned, completed and occupied including the State of Maharashtra till date;
(c) the number of houses sanctioned, completed and occupied under PMAY-U 2.0, district-wise; and
(d) the details of the steps taken to improve urban infrastructure, including transport, sanitation systems, water supply and housing in Tier-II and Tier-III cities and their surrounding areas?

(a) the status of completion of projects under the Smart Cities Mission (SCM) in the State of Maharashtra as on date during the current financial year;
(b) the details of fund utilisation, project completion rates and citizen feedback systems implemented in these cities;
(c) whether projects under the Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) 2.0 have been delayed due to land-related issues or shortage of contractors, if so, the details thereof in respect of the State of Maharashtra; and
(d) whether there is any plan to support Tier-3 cities with regard to digital governance and sanitation infrastructure through upcoming urban reform schemes?
